			<h3 class="result-heading">Why warm-start the action trajectory?</h3>
			<p class="project-abstract">
				With fresh synchronous vision, PFWS lowers episode-averaged boundary flips from 2.57% to
				1.36% over 500 paired starts, and boundary excess from +0.88 to −0.03 percentage points. The
				paper finds its clearest contribution in continuity; the paired evidence for native success
				gains is inconclusive. In a shared PCA projection, warm-started paths begin closer to the
				endpoint, reducing one-step endpoint error by 19.7% without changing the expert.
			</p>
