					<strong>Fig. 5.</strong> Frozen-expert flow paths projected into a shared PCA basis for eight
					matched seeds. Circles mark initial latents and squares mark dense endpoints; these are projections
					rather than physical robot trajectories.
				</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<h3 class="result-heading">Robustness and component ablations</h3>
			<p class="project-abstract">
				Across 2,519 LIBERO-Plus variants, PFWS increases overall success from 76.38% to 78.09%
				within CauSyncVLA, but it does not help every shift. Noise and robot-state changes benefit
				from trajectory reuse; viewpoint and layout changes can favor cold starts. The synchronous
				PFWS reference achieves 80.15% overall, so these results do not establish unconditional
				robustness over fresh vision.
			</p>
			<figure class="result-figure">
				<div class="figure-media">
					{
						corners.map((corner) => (
							<span class={`figure-cross figure-cross--${corner}`} aria-hidden="true">
								+
