				</div>
				<figcaption>
					<strong>Fig. 6.</strong> PFWS success differences versus cold starts, in percentage points,
					across LIBERO-Plus perturbations for synchronous vision and CauSyncVLA with a fixed world model.
				</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<p class="project-abstract result-copy">
				In matched module ablations, removing the world model lowers success to 80.20%, while
				removing PFWS increases pooled flips to 3.69%. The full matched control reaches 93.40% with
				1.86% flips. In a separate matched objective comparison, adding action distillation reduces
				action MSE from 0.02018 to 0.00983 and raises success from 85.60% to 92.80%, despite a
				higher KV error. This supports supervising control-relevant memory directions, not just
				minimizing uniform KV distance. These matched cohorts differ from the 93.80% main-result
				run.
			</p>
